# Agent work-package verification

Apply when implementing a GitHub issue labeled `agent-ready` or filed from **Agent work package**.

## Before coding

1. Run **`npm run agent:issue:ready -- <n>`** (≤15-line stdout). If exit 1, comment `blocked: not Ready` and stop. Do **not** re-read full Ready prose unless the script is unclear.
2. Read the **issue body** (source of truth). Open `docs/sdlc/agent-async-delivery-program.md` only if blocked on process.
3. Restate scope briefly (goal, issue, in-scope, out-of-scope, acceptance, verification).

## During coding

- **One issue → one branch → one PR.** Do not expand into sibling wave packages.
- Every edge-case matrix row needs a test, simulator step, or explicit N/A + reason before Done.
- Prefer shared `fixtures/pacing/*` over ad-hoc samples.
- **Handoff:** feature agents put a ≤5-line **Handoff delta** in the PR; only the **integration agent** edits `docs/sdlc/agent-handoff.md`.
- Mid-slice prefer `npm run verify:api|mobile|contracts`; full `npm run verify` before PR.
- Respect path conflict map; if another PR owns the same paths, wait or coordinate via issue comment.

## Before claiming Done

- `npm run verify` green locally.
- Mobile UI: `npm run agent:ios:ready` (+ `--deeplink crewcue://dev/...` Auth0-free) + simulator QA; evidence on PR only.
- `npm run agent:pr:done -- <pr>` (or `--body-file` before open) must exit 0.
- PR: `Closes #<n>` + edge-case proofs. Never fake a pass when blocked.
